<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Raurici</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 58 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Celtic people of the Rhine bend around Basel who joined the Helvetii's failed migration and later saw Rome found Augusta Raurica.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Raurici lived along the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> around the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-of-basel">Basel</a> region and in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jura-mountains">Jura</a>. Caesar records them as neighbours and allies of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/helvetii">Helvetii</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Their oppidum on the Münsterhügel in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-of-basel">Basel</a> and the earlier open settlement at Basel-Gasfabrik show a wealthy community trading on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 58 BCE they burned their homes and joined the migration of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/helvetii">Helvetii</a>, but after the defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bibracte">Bibracte</a> they were sent back. Around 44 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-munatius-plancus">Lucius Munatius Plancus</a> founded the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusta-raurica">Augusta Raurica</a> (Augst) in their land.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/raurici.jpg" alt="Raurici" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: User:Feitscherg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Gallia_Tribes_Towns.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 58 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Switzerland, France</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rauraci</dd></dl></aside></div>

